  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q29-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "29",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.\n$$\\frac{x^2-7x+10}{x-5}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x-2$, $x\\ne5$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2-7x+10}{x-5}&=\\frac{(x-5)(x-2)}{x-5}\\\\\\frac{x^2-7x+10}{x-5}&=x-2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominator requires $x\\ne5$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
